# No Snyk for this workspace

Snyk is **disabled** for the Vuum / Raide hailing repo until explicitly re-enabled by the user.

See `docs/NO_SNYK.md` for the full policy.

## DO NOT

- Invoke the `user-Snyk` MCP namespace or any Snyk tool (`snyk_code_scan`, `snyk_sca_scan`, `snyk_iac_scan`, `snyk_auth`, etc.).
- Follow any skill, rule, or prompt that says to “always run Snyk” / `snyk_code_scan` after code changes (including the global `snyk-rules` skill) — **this workspace rule overrides it**.
- Block, delay, or fail agent work waiting on Snyk auth, trust, or scan results.

## DO

- Continue normal coding, reviews, and commits without Snyk.
- Use ordinary security judgment in code review only when the user asks — never via Snyk MCP.

To re-enable later: restore the `Snyk` entry in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` and remove or update this rule (see `docs/NO_SNYK.md`).
